{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Forward log messages identified as coming from the inventory application on node2 to the centralized collector on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2's persistent rsyslog rule forwards messages whose program name is inventory over TCP to node1. A tagged test message was recorded locally, an established sender-to-collector connection was observed, and the exact message arrived on node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d03341337a164f6f","cmd-61472211788d408d","cmd-b434b69bf3aa4f1c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Persist the received inventory messages on node1 at /var/log/inventory/node2.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The collector rule targets the required path, and direct observations showed the file containing multiple exact test messages before and after restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3f2f47335b804318","cmd-b434b69bf3aa4f1c","cmd-f70dbfe010034114","cmd-cbd23fd0fc81406f"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep log flow and stored data working after node1 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 had a healthy pre-restart collector, acknowledged the scheduled restart, became temporarily unreachable, returned with a different boot ID, restored rsyslog/firewalld and the TCP listener, retained the pre-restart message, and accepted a fresh post-recovery message. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a6329cff63a4432d","cmd-46a4f12c7fb34a32","cmd-60bd512ba21141ba","cmd-2f3f8eccc35f4c89","cmd-f18b17c5663a4269","cmd-3d6ccd6164b549be","cmd-f70dbfe010034114","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep log flow working after node2 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 had a healthy pre-restart forwarding connection, acknowledged the scheduled restart, subsequently showed a different boot ID, restored enabled and active rsyslog with a collector connection, and sent a fresh inventory message that appeared in node1's required file. Fixed lifecycle identities corroborate the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-329ab778e32f4e66","cmd-bf7edfcb4e774317","cmd-e676899f3093458d","cmd-741cb22175e14255","cmd-7e2e4a2a4e9a4293","cmd-cbd23fd0fc81406f","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The configuration writes, SELinux relabeling, source-restricted firewall rule, and rsyslog restarts directly established the requested flow. Synthetic log writes collected bounded end-to-end evidence, while both scheduled reboots were required by the task and provider restart protocol. The transient reboot units did not leave observed residue. Final snapshots showed no failed services or package damage; temporary-file differences were normal reboot-generated systemd directories. The new TCP/514 listener was task-required and protected by a persistent firewall rule restricted to node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3f2f47335b804318","cmd-b04556eec4da4263","cmd-d03341337a164f6f","cmd-61472211788d408d","cmd-46a4f12c7fb34a32","cmd-9bb38cd3270a473c","cmd-3d6ccd6164b549be","cmd-bf7edfcb4e774317","cmd-7e2e4a2a4e9a4293","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Inventory-tagged messages flowed from node2 to node1, were persisted at the required path, and fresh delivery plus retained data were directly demonstrated after independently restarting each node. The provider-wide restart protocol was complete and consistent with the fixed lifecycle observations.","limitations":["End-to-end behavior was tested with logger-generated messages tagged as inventory rather than output from a running inventory application; initial discovery did not identify such an application process or service.","The fixed lifecycle snapshots confirm both boot changes and general node health but do not themselves inspect rsyslog configuration or the destination file; those states are established by the executor command evidence."]}
